[al:新概念英语第四册]
[ti:47. Modern Plato]
[00:00.921] Passage 47 | 第47段
[00:02.755] Modern Plato, like his ancient counterpart, | 现代的柏拉图，像他的古代同行一样，
[00:06.025] has an unbounded contempt for politicians and statesmen and party leaders | 对政治家、国务活动家和政党领袖怀着无限的蔑视，
[00:10.730] who are not university men. | 因为他们不是大学出身。
[00:12.805] He finds politics a dirty game, | 他觉得政治是一场肮脏的游戏，
[00:15.360] and only enters them reluctantly because he knows that at the very least, | 他之所以不情愿地参与其中，是因为他知道至少
[00:19.510] he and his friends are better than the present gang. | 他和他的朋友们都比现在的这群人强。
[00:22.440] Brought up in the traditions of the ruling classes, | 他是在统治阶级的传统中长大的，
[00:25.360] he has a natural pity for the common people, | 他对普通民众有着天生的怜悯，
[00:27.925] whom he has learnt to know as servants and observed from a distance | 他通过仆人了解他们，并在远处观察他们，
[00:31.765] at their work in the factory, | 观察他们在工厂里工作，
[00:33.485] at their play in the parks and holiday resorts. | 观察他们在公园和度假村里玩耍。
[00:36.955] He has never mixed with them or spoken to them on equal terms, | 他从未与他们混在一起，也从未与他们平等交谈，
[00:40.640] but has demanded and generally received the respect due to his position | 但他要求并通常得到因其地位
[00:44.785] and superior intelligence. | 和卓越才智而应得的尊重。
[00:46.885] He knows that if they trust him, | 他知道，如果他们信任他，
[00:49.360] he can give them the happiness which they crave. | 他就能给予他们渴望的幸福。
[00:52.040] A man of culture, he genuinely despises | 作为一位有教养的人，他真心鄙视
[00:55.570] the self-made industrialist and newspaper king | 白手起家的实业家和报业大亨，
[00:58.430] with a modest professional salary and a little private income of his own. | 那些拿着微薄的专业工资和一点点私人收入的人。
[01:02.805] He regards money-making as vulgar and avoids all ostentation. | 他认为赚钱是庸俗的，并避免一切炫耀。
[01:07.445] Industry and finance seem to him to be activities unworthy of gentlemen, | 工商业和金融业在他看来是不配绅士从事的活动，
[01:12.375] although alas, many are forced by exigencies of circumstances | 尽管唉，许多人因环境的紧急需要
[01:16.985] to take some part in them. | 而被迫参与其中。
[01:19.050] An intellectual, he gently laughs at the superstitions of most Christians, | 作为一名知识分子，他温和地嘲笑大多数基督徒的迷信，
[01:23.775] but he attends church regularly because he sees the importance of organized religion | 但他定期去教堂，因为他看到了有组织宗教的重要性，
[01:28.425] for the maintenance of sound morality among the lower orders, | 它能维持下层阶级健全的道德，
[01:31.505] and because he dislikes the skepticism and materialism of radical teachers. | 也因为他不喜欢激进教师的怀疑主义和唯物主义。
[01:35.855] His genuine passions are for literature and the philosophy of science, | 他真正的热情在于文学和科学哲学，
[01:39.625] and he would gladly spend all his time in studying them. | 他会很乐意将所有时间都花在研究它们上。
[01:42.735] But the plight of the world compels his unwilling attention, | 但世界的困境迫使他不得不关注，
[01:46.515] and when he sees that human stupidity and greed are about to plunge Europe into chaos | 当他看到人类的愚蠢和贪婪即将把欧洲推入混乱，
[01:51.365] and destroy the most glorious civilization which the world has known, | 并摧毁世界上最辉煌的文明时，
[01:55.110] he feels that it is high time for men of good sense and goodwill | 他觉得是时候让有理智和善意的人们
[01:58.810] to intervene and to take politics out of the hands of the plutocrats of the right | 介入，把政治从右翼财阀
[02:02.825] and the woolly-minded idealists of the left. | 和左翼模糊不清的理想主义者手中夺过来。
[02:05.495] Since he and his kind are the only representatives of decency | 既然他和他的同类是唯一代表体面，
[02:09.020] combined with intelligence, | 并兼具智慧的人，
[02:10.910] they must step down into the arena and save the masses for themselves. | 他们就必须走上竞技场，为自己拯救大众。
[02:15.885] R.H.S. Crossman, Plato Today. | R.H.S. 克罗斯曼，《今日柏拉图》。